Got it 👍 — this is a very common (and good) validation case.

Right now, when the sheet name from the Config does NOT exist in the evaluation file, you’re just skipping that mapping:

If srcWS Is Nothing Then GoTo NextMap

But what you want is:

> ❌ If ANY required sheet name is missing → move the whole file to INVALID




---

✅ Recommended Logic (Best Practice)

Rule:
If at least one required config sheet (for that material type) is missing →
➡ stop processing
➡ close the file
➡ move it to Invalid


---

🔧 Minimal, Clean Fix (Fits Your Current Code)

1️⃣ Add a flag at the top of the file loop

Dim hasMissingSheet As Boolean
hasMissingSheet = False

Place this after hasMismatch = False.


---

2️⃣ Detect missing sheet and mark file as invalid

Replace this part:

On Error Resume Next
Set srcWS = evalWB.Sheets(srcSheetName)
On Error GoTo 0

If srcWS Is Nothing Then GoTo NextMap

✅ With this:

Set srcWS = Nothing
On Error Resume Next
Set srcWS = evalWB.Sheets(srcSheetName)
On Error GoTo 0

If srcWS Is Nothing Then
    hasMissingSheet = True
    Exit For   ' stop config loop immediately
End If

✔ No GoTo
✔ Faster
✔ Clear intent


---

3️⃣ After config loop, move file to INVALID if needed

Right after:

Next r

Add this block:

If hasMissingSheet Then
    evalWB.Close SaveChanges:=False
    
    ' Archive old invalid files
    ArchiveExistingByPrefix invalidFolder, archiveFolder, supplierCode
    
    file.Move invalidFolder & evalfile
    GoTo NextFile   ' skip Completed logic
End If


---

4️⃣ Add loop label at bottom

Change:

Next file

To:

NextFile:
Next file


---

🧠 What This Achieves

Scenario	Result

Sheet name exists	✅ Process normally
Sheet missing	❌ File → Invalid
Partial mapping	❌ File → Invalid
Prevents partial writes	✅ Yes


This is exactly how enterprise validation should work.


